<title>GERMANY: Hoechst to contribute 6.5 bln sales to new group.</title>
<headline>Hoechst to contribute 6.5 bln sales to new group.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group Hoechst AG said it will contribute 6.5 billion marks in annual sales to a new speciality chemical group, created through a merger with Swiss group Clariant AG.</p>
<p>The Swiss group will contribute 2.7 billion marks in sales and 8,500 employees to the venture, which is expected to post annual sales of some nine billion marks.</p>
<p>Hoechst said the Clariant merger is to save hundreds of millions of Swiss francs in costs.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
